09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # ONE dumpsys battery, three fields. Temperature alone cannot answer "what did
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # this arm cost the battery" — Charge counter is the coulomb counter (uAh,
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # falling while discharging) and is the only field here that integrates energy.
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # It sits in the same output the probe was already paying for and was thrown
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # away. grep -m1 takes the service-state block, which dumpsys prints before the
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): # ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED history lines that repeat these same key names.
09-09 08:02:06.748 I/adbd    (10663): battery_dump=$(dumpsys battery 2>/dev/null || true)
